course: dictionary
lesson: 7377
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Plot is one word with several meanings, so the sentence around it is your best clue. In a story lesson it means the events of the story. «Every story has characters, a setting and a plot.» Here the plot is what happens.
explain: In maths, plot is a verb: to plot points means to mark them on a grid. «Plot the points (2, 3) on the grid.» In the garden, a plot is a small piece of land: «Dad grows carrots on his vegetable plot.» Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: Plot can also mean a secret plan to do something wrong, or the verb to plan something secretly. Lily thinks Arjun is plotting, but his mate explains the staring another way. Check the clues before you decide what a word means in a sentence.
fact: Plot, as a noun, means the main events of a story, film or play.
fact: The plot thickens is a phrase meaning the story is getting more complicated and exciting.
fact: In 1605 a plot tried to blow up Parliament, and in Britain we remember it every 5 November on Bonfire Night.
fact: Lost the plot is British slang meaning gone mad or behaving in a wild, senseless way.
fact: To plot points means to mark them on a graph or map.
exercise: «Every story has characters, a setting and a plot.» In this sentence, what is the plot? | *What happens in the story | The names of the people | The place and time | A small piece of land
exercise: «Plot the points (2, 3) on the grid.» What does plot mean here? | To make a film | To plan something secretly | To dig a small garden | *To mark points on a graph
exercise: «Dad grows carrots on his vegetable plot.» What is a plot here? | A story | A graph | *A piece of land | A secret plan
test: In 1605 a plot tried to blow up Parliament. What is a plot here? | *A secret plan to do something wrong | The main events of a film | To mark points on a graph | A small piece of land
test: Lily thinks Arjun is plotting, but his mate says «He fancies you». What does this teach us? | *Check the clues before you decide what someone means | Plotting always means something bad | Mates never give good advice | Starers are always enemies
exam: «Lost the plot» is British slang. What does it mean? | *Gone mad or behaving in a wild, senseless way | Forgot the time | Lost a page of a book | Found a garden plot
